    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d531">

                <pb facs="0734" n="640" sameAs="frus:frus1896/pg640"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Rockhill to Mr.
                            Taylor.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1896-06-24"><hi rendition="#italic">June 24,
                        1896</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 527.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to the Department’s No. 505, of
                    the 13th ultimo, I inclose copy of No. 120<anchor n="l" xml:id="d531-f1"/>, of
                    the 10th instant, from our commercial agent at Sagua la Grande, reporting that
                    Messrs. William A. and Louis M. Glean are still held on parole, subject to
                    military jurisdiction, and that the nature of the charge of which they are
                    accused has not been made known to them.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">W. W. Rockhill</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Acting Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
